{"slug":"count-signs","title":"Count Positive, Negative and Zero","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"easy","order":101,"tags":["arrays","counting"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"One pass, a few counters","body":["Many array questions need only a single pass: walk over the elements once and update a few variables. Here three counters are enough, one for each kind of number.",{"code":"pos = neg = zero = 0\nfor x in a:\n    if x > 0:\n        pos += 1\n    elif x < 0:\n        neg += 1\n    else:\n        zero += 1"},"Every number is exactly one of the three kinds, so `if / elif / else` is the natural choice and the counters always add up to `n`."]},"statement":["You are given `n` integers. Count how many of them are positive, how many are negative and how many are zero."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","The second line has `n` integers."],"outputFormat":["Print three integers separated by spaces: the number of positives, negatives and zeros."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","-10^9 <= each number <= 10^9"],"examples":[{"input":"6\n3 -1 0 7 -5 0\n","output":"2 2 2\n","note":"Two positive, two negative and two zeros."}],"hints":["Go through the array once.","Keep three counters and add one to the right counter for each number.","Use `if x > 0`, `elif x < 0` and `else` (the zeros)."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["One pass with three counters. Each number increases exactly one of them."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(1).","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\npos = neg = zero = 0\nfor x in a:\n    if x > 0:\n        pos += 1\n    elif x < 0:\n        neg += 1\n    else:\n        zero += 1\nprint(pos, neg, zero)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    int pos = 0, neg = 0, zero = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (a[i] > 0) pos++;\n        else if (a[i] < 0) neg++;\n        else zero++;\n    }\n    cout << pos << \" \" << neg << \" \" << zero << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        int pos = 0, neg = 0, zero = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (a[i] > 0) pos++;\n            else if (a[i] < 0) neg++;\n            else zero++;\n        }\n        System.out.println(pos + \" \" + neg + \" \" + zero);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"1\n0\n","output":"0 0 1\n"},{"input":"1\n-7\n","output":"0 1 0\n"},{"input":"3\n0 0 0\n","output":"0 0 3\n"},{"input":"4\n5 6 7 8\n","output":"4 0 0\n"},{"input":"4\n-5 -6 -7 -8\n","output":"0 4 0\n"},{"input":"20\n-3 2 0 1 -1 1 1 3 -2 -3 -1 2 -1 3 0 -3 -3 -1 -3 -2\n","output":"7 11 2\n"},{"input":"1000\n521099364 -457507659 -886720122 294425727 -915486815 180715307 -894714892 -128521608 720273657 -129575283 492457201 841051990 254689519 -863444494 -682767860 -708645740 31738291 -998104848 285009690 -754741730 -652888662 -918093671 915951482 -135439276 -707600076 539644365 -3266937